From: OpenHarmony PC porting (libomptarget-rtl-amdgpu 18.1.8)
Subject: [PATCH] openmp/runtime: no pthread_cancel on OpenHarmony (musl)

OpenHarmony's musl removes the pthread cancellation API: pthread_cancel,
pthread_setcanceltype and pthread_setcancelstate are absent from the OHOS
sysroot <pthread.h>, so z_Linux_util.cpp fails to compile wherever
KMP_CANCEL_THREADS is defined.

Follow the existing Android/WASI precedent in this file and undefine
KMP_CANCEL_THREADS on __OHOS__ so the guarded call sites compile out.
No behavior change on any other platform.

--- a/openmp/runtime/src/kmp.h
+++ b/openmp/runtime/src/kmp.h
@@ -68,6 +68,13 @@
 #if KMP_OS_WASI
 #undef KMP_CANCEL_THREADS
 #endif
+// OpenHarmony (OHOS) musl removes the pthread cancellation API
+// (pthread_cancel/pthread_setcancel{type,state}); guard the call sites
+// out the same way as Android and WASI above.
+#if defined(__OHOS__)
+#undef KMP_CANCEL_THREADS
+#endif
+
 
 #if !KMP_OS_WASI
 #include <signal.h>
